<title>FRANCE: GAN shares requote 21.2 pct up in Paris.</title>
<headline>GAN shares requote 21.2 pct up in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French state-controlled insurer Groupe des Assurances Nationales requoted 21.22 percent higher when they requoted on the stock exchange on Friday after three temporary suspensions following the announcement on Thursday of a 20-billion-franc state rescue package.</p>
<p>The stock was suspended on Thursday at a level of 123 francs and was temporarily suspended twice at the open on Friday under stock market &quot;time out&quot; regulations which halt trading for 15 minutes when a share soars more than 10 percent.</p>
<p>The stock was later suspended limit up indefinitely.</p>
</text>
